  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with the Article III of the SBAA [or the Supplemental Provisions to the Project Document], the responsibility for the safety and security of the Implementing Partner and its personnel and property, and of UNDP&#x2019;s property in the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s custody, rests with the Implementing Partner.  To this end, the Implementing Partner shall: a)	put in place an appropriate security plan and maintain the security plan, taking into account the security situation in the country where the project is being carried; b)	assume all risks and liabilities related to the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s security, and the full implementation of the security plan.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and environmental sustainability will be enhanced through application of the UNDP Social and Environmental Standards (http://www.undp.org/ses) and related Accountability Mechanism (http://www.undp.org/secu-srm).</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Project launched
- Office established
- Operational manual prepared</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2014">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Total hectares legally designated as a national protected area conforming to basic IUCN standards/categories: Terrestrial: 92728 ha Marine: 51428 ha</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Policy and Institutional Framework to operationalize the National Protected Area System has been finalized. This framework is instrumental in facilitating establishment of protected area systems at the local, regional, and national levels.
The proposed protected area system is yet be designated as a national protected area conforming to basic IUCN standards/categories. In the meantime, however, using current management practice, 91,143 is considered critical habitat of the Semenawi and Debubawi Bahri are under strict conservation management.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Total hectares of critical habitat conserved within newly established national protected areas.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">No new bio-physical measures were implemented this year. However, continued follow- up and proper management of the lands that have been developed in the preceding years have been successfully implemented. Through this action 163,625 hectares of land and marine habitats and 11,8505 hectares are under sustainable 163,625 hectares of land and marine habitats and 11,8505 hectares are under sustainable forest /range-lands management.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Total hectares of critical habitat conserved within newly established national protected areas.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through UNDP technical and financial support, 1,000 hectares of land were managed sustainably under sustainable landscape restoration and conservation and climate-resilient agricultural practices. The ecosystem-based solutions included a range of natural resources conservation and restoration including construction of hillsides, on-farm terraces, and check-dams, planting of various tree species, and temporary and permanent strict closures. Moreover, about 14,000 hectares of marine and terrestrial habitats continued to be under strict protection and sustainable forest management.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
